# GloBell — Starting Niches

**Version:** 0.1  
**Status:** Concept / Potential Launch Strategy

---

## 1. Why Starting Niches Matter

The first users are the hardest users to acquire for a location-based network.

A new network has an obvious problem:

> There is little value in joining a network in which nobody is present yet.

GloBell should therefore avoid starting with the entire world.

The initial objective is to enter an environment where a meaningful social network already exists and where people already have recurring needs connected with location.

The principle is:

```text
Existing community
        ↓
Existing trust
        ↓
Existing local needs
        ↓
GloBell
        ↓
First active network
